Patchlevel 7 will be released to comp.sources.games for distribution
on Monday.

Apart from, literally, hundreds of bugfixes and local enhancements, Pl7
will contain advanced VMS, Amiga, Mac, and PC Overlay ports, as well as
a port to the HP.

The delay in releasing Pl7 resulted, in part, from encountering 
recalcitrant mysterious bugs in an even _more_ advanced Overlay scheme 
on which the PC group has been working.  Incredible amounts of time and 
energy were invested by Pierre, Stephen, Norm, and Kevins in an effort 
to kill these bugs in time for the Pl7 release, but thus far these efforts 
yielded only a partial success.  

The Overlay scheme being developed is very complex, and working on it 
requires a great deal of time and patience.  That work cannot be done 
under the gun of a deadline.  Therefore, we decided 

	(a) to include in Pl7 an _interim_ advanced version which has proven 
itself stable and which is a great improvement over the one in Pl6,
	(b) to continue the development of the new Overlay at a comfortable
pace, and when completed,
	(c) to release the results in a Patchlevel 8, which will be devoted
almost exclusively to ports enhancements.

This will also provide an opportunity to you to test and help us debug (if
needed) the Mac and Amiga ports which contain many new features.  Any needed
changes in these ports will be included in Pl8.

While the PC group works on debugging the Overlay port, the Development Team 
will commence working on NetHack 3.1.

For the Development Team,

-Izchak


